# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() stops a sleeping strand tagged with that tag;
#         concurrent variants: stop before vs after strand starts sleeping.
# blocked: top-level & separator hangs chk driver (T39)
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason:
#   tag.stop() is called as an object method on a UTag value (e.g., tag.stop()).
#   Method dispatch on prototype values is a M4 object-model feature.  At M3
#   we have urbi_tag_stop() as a C API but no urbiscript-level dispatch.  The
#   fixture also uses '&' for concurrent stop vs sleep — requires M5 chk driver.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with tag method dispatch):
# # var tag = Tag.new() | {};
# # tag: { {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} & tag.stop() };
# # tag: { tag.stop() & {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} };
